{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A checkout changed during a stoppage can be published using a passing result from a different commit."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A restart during a retry can remove dependencies and cause a false blocking regression because setup is skipped."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An injected executor's events are dropped, losing progress and logs while its final result still controls the outcome."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A command containing a registered credential can lose its retry or fail on replay because redacted text replaces the executable command."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A reusable executor can repeatedly return a retained infrastructure failure instead of starting a fresh attempt."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Standalone retry helpers now share scratch state across checks, but only tests currently call them without the engine's existing shared scope."}]}